# TypeScript conventions

## Types first

All domain types live in `lib/types/core.ts`. Define interfaces there before writing implementations. Every function signature uses these types. No `any` for domain concepts.

Core types: `ChunkMetadata`, `Citation`, `Metric`, `InvestmentAnalysis`, `AnalysisState`, `ExtractedMetric`, `RetrievedChunk`.

## Naming

- **Files:** kebab-case (`analysis.service.ts`, `retrieve.ts`)
- **Interfaces/types:** PascalCase (`InvestmentAnalysis`, `ChunkMetadata`)
- **Functions:** camelCase, verb-first (`ingestDocument`, `retrieveChunks`, `embedChunks`)
- **Path alias:** `@/` → project root

## DI (tsyringe)

Services and repositories use `@injectable()`. Resolve via `container.resolve(X)` in API routes and server components. Register in `lib/di/setup.ts`.

Plain async functions: `lib/ingestion/` and `lib/retrieval/` — no DI, no classes.

## Async patterns

- Await everything in the request path.
- Background work (ingestion after upload): `.catch(err => console.error(err))` — the only fire-and-forget permitted.
- Atomic DB writes: `withTransaction` from `lib/repositories/base.repository.ts`. Only needed for `analyses` and `conversations`.

## Error handling

- Throw domain error subclasses from `lib/errors/domain-errors.ts`.
- API routes: `handleError(error)` → `{ message, statusCode }`.
- Server actions: return `{ success: true, data } | { success: false, error: string }`.
- Zod at every API boundary.

## No `any`

- LLM outputs: use Zod `withStructuredOutput`.
- Pinecone metadata: cast through `ChunkMetadata`.
- DB jsonb columns (`analyses.result`, `analyses.documents`, `conversations.messages`): define typed interfaces and cast at the boundary with `as`.
- `(workflow as any).addEdge("__start__", ...)` — single allowed exception, LangGraph v0.2 API requirement.

## React / Next.js

- Server Components by default; `"use client"` only for interactivity.
- `params`/`searchParams` are `Promise<...>` in Next 15 — always `await` them.
- `export const dynamic = "force-dynamic"` on all authenticated dashboard pages.
- Toasts: `sonner`. Auth: `@clerk/nextjs` (`auth()` server, `useAuth()` client).

## Comments

Only for non-obvious constraints. Never narrate what code does.
